#!/bin/sh
# postinst of minisforum-n5-it5571-dkms: take over a hand installation
# (deploy/install.sh), register the source with DKMS, build and install the
# module for every kernel that has headers, load it once when it is not.
set -e
PKG=minisforum-n5-it5571
VER=@VERSION@
MOD=minisforum_n5_it5571
# sha256 of the two /etc files deploy/install.sh wrote before this package
# existed; an identical copy is removed (the /usr/lib file applies), an
# edited one is kept (it overrides the /usr/lib file).
LEGACY_MODPROBE=5329370f77fb68e1eaa4e73be5613ac0cae7a82b2240d8993d3e8d3d4a652b70
LEGACY_LOAD=f346cbe2a9cea0372632c7aac1b01db4f54392f46a09f9dd6b1e54cbd076729e

say() { echo "$PKG: $*"; }

adopt_hand_install() {
	for d in /usr/src/$PKG-*; do
		[ -d "$d" ] || continue
		v=${d#/usr/src/$PKG-}
		[ "$v" = "$VER" ] && continue
		dpkg-query -S "$d" >/dev/null 2>&1 && continue # another package owns it
		say "taking over the hand-installed DKMS source $v (deploy/install.sh)"
		dkms remove -m $PKG -v "$v" --all >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
		rm -rf "$d"
	done
	for pair in "/etc/modprobe.d/$PKG.conf $LEGACY_MODPROBE" "/etc/modules-load.d/$PKG.conf $LEGACY_LOAD"; do
		set -- $pair
		[ -f "$1" ] || continue
		if [ "$(sha256sum "$1" | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$2" ]; then
			rm -f "$1"
			say "removed the hand-installed $1; /usr/lib${1#/etc} applies"
		else
			say "keeping $1 (edited); it overrides /usr/lib${1#/etc}"
		fi
	done
}

case "$1" in
configure)
	adopt_hand_install
	dkms status -m $PKG -v $VER 2>/dev/null | grep -q . || dkms add -m $PKG -v $VER >/dev/null
	running=$(uname -r)
	failed_running=0
	for m in /lib/modules/*; do
		[ -d "$m" ] || continue
		k=${m##*/}
		if [ ! -e "$m/build" ]; then
			if [ "$k" = "$running" ]; then
				say "WARNING: no headers for the running kernel $k — install proxmox-headers-$k (or linux-headers-$k)" >&2
			fi
			continue
		fi
		log=$(mktemp)
		if dkms install -m $PKG -v $VER -k "$k" --force >"$log" 2>&1; then
			say "built and installed for $k"
		else
			say "build FAILED for $k:" >&2
			tail -n 15 "$log" >&2
			[ "$k" = "$running" ] && failed_running=1
		fi
		rm -f "$log"
	done
	[ $failed_running -eq 0 ] || exit 1
	if lsmod 2>/dev/null | grep -q "^$MOD "; then
		say "module already loaded; the new build takes effect after 'modprobe -r $MOD && modprobe $MOD' (stop the regulator first) or the next boot"
	elif modprobe $MOD 2>/dev/null; then
		say "module loaded"
	else
		say "module not loaded now (no matching N5 Pro, or no permission here); it loads at boot via /usr/lib/modules-load.d/$PKG.conf"
	fi
	;;
esac
exit 0
